#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:6
msgid "Managing Agents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:8
msgid ""
"Mattermost Agents V2 turns agent management into a first-class product "
"surface. Each agent is a database-backed identity with its own bot user "
"account, instructions, model, access rules, and MCP tool grants. This "
"guide explains where agents live in the product, who can manage them, and"
" how to create, edit, and delete them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:10
msgid ""
"For broader plugin configuration (services, web search, embedding search,"
" MCP servers, per-tool policies), see the [Admin "
"Guide](../admin_guide.md). For chat usage and tool approval flows, see "
"the [User Guide](../user_guide.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:12
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:14
msgid ""
"In v2, an agent is more than a JSON entry in plugin config. Each agent "
"has:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:16
msgid ""
"A persistent record in the `Agents_UserAgents` database table. Migrations"
" `000005` and `000006` create the table and add the model, native-tool, "
"reasoning, and structured-output columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:17
msgid ""
"A linked Mattermost bot account. Display name and avatar updates on the "
"agent flow through to that bot account; deleting an agent deactivates the"
" bot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:18
msgid ""
"A creator (`CreatorID`) and an optional list of agent admins "
"(`AdminUserIDs`). The creator is always an admin and can't be removed "
"from that role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:19
msgid ""
"Channel and user access rules and an MCP tool allowlist (or \"all MCP "
"tools\" auto-grant) stored on the same record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:20
msgid ""
"Cluster-aware change propagation: when an agent is created, edited, or "
"deleted, the originating node refreshes its bot cache, publishes a "
"`agent_update` cluster event, and broadcasts a `bots_invalidate` "
"websocket event so every node and connected client picks up the change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:22
msgid ""
"This means agent identity, instructions, scoping, and tool grants are "
"part of your Mattermost data — they live in the same database as your "
"channels and users, are covered by your normal Mattermost backups, and "
"survive plugin restarts and upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:24
msgid "Where Agents live in the product"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:26
msgid ""
"Agents is a top-level Mattermost product entry, not a plugin panel. It "
"registers itself with the Mattermost product switcher (the grid icon) so "
"the Agents page renders inside the Mattermost shell with full theming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:28
msgid "You can reach the Agents page in three ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:30
msgid "Use the **product switcher** (grid icon) and select **Agents**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:31
msgid "Open the URL `/plug/mattermost-ai/agents` directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:32
msgid "From a conversation, open **AI Actions > Manage agents**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:34
msgid ""
"The **System Console > AI Bots** page no longer hosts the agent editor. "
"Instead, it shows an **AI bot configuration has moved** notice with a "
"link back to the Agents page. System administrators can still set the "
"default bot in the same System Console section, just below the redirect "
"notice — but creating, editing, and deleting agents happens on the Agents"
" page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:36
msgid "The Agents page itself shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:38
msgid ""
"A header with the page title and a **Create agent** button (visible only "
"to users who can create agents — see [Permissions and license"
"](#permissions-and-license))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:39
msgid ""
"Two tabs: **All agents** (every agent the user can see) and **Your "
"agents** (agents the current user created)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:40
msgid "A search box that filters by display name or username."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:41
msgid ""
"One row per agent showing the avatar, display name, `@username`, an **All"
" MCP tools** or **N tools** badge, and a **Service unavailable** warning "
"badge if the agent's configured AI service is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:42
msgid ""
"A row-level overflow menu (`⋯`) with **Edit** and **Delete** actions for "
"users who can manage that agent. Selecting the row itself also opens the "
"editor for users who can manage the agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:44
msgid "Permissions and license"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:46
msgid ""
"Agent management uses three Mattermost system permissions plus a license "
"check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:48
msgid "Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "Permission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "Capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "`manage_own_agent`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "Create new agents and edit/delete agents the user is an admin of."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "`manage_others_agent`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Edit and delete any agent on the server, including agents the user did "
"not create."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "`manage_system`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"System administrator. Always allowed to manage agents that have no "
"creator (migrated legacy bots) and may create agents in the absence of "
"`manage_own_agent`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:56
msgid ""
"The Agents page applies these rules consistently between the UI and the "
"API:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:58
msgid ""
"The **Create agent** button is shown to users with `manage_own_agent` or "
"`manage_system`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:59
msgid "A row's **Edit/Delete** actions are available to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:60
msgid "The agent's creator,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:61
msgid "Anyone listed in the agent's **Agent admins** field,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:62
msgid "Anyone with `manage_others_agent`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:63
msgid ""
"System administrators, when the agent has no creator (a migrated legacy "
"bot — see [Legacy bot migration](#legacy-bot-migration))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:64
msgid ""
"The same checks gate the underlying `POST /agents`, `PUT /agents/:id`, "
"and `DELETE /agents/:id` API routes, so direct API calls cannot bypass "
"the UI rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:66
msgid ""
"By default, regular users do not have `manage_own_agent`. Grant it "
"through your existing Mattermost role/permission model to delegate agent "
"creation — typically under **System Console > User Management > "
"Permissions** (exact path varies by Mattermost server version)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:68
msgid "License"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:70
msgid ""
"Self-service agent creation is gated by Mattermost's multi-LLM license "
"check (Entry, Enterprise, or Enterprise Advanced)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:72
msgid ""
"**Without a multi-LLM license**, the Agents page shows a **Self-Service "
"Agents** upgrade screen with a link to Mattermost pricing instead of the "
"agent list. The plugin enforces a limit of `1` self-service agent at the "
"API level (the `FreeTierAgentLimit` constant in `api/api_agents.go`), but"
" **there is no UI path to create it** — agent creation requires a "
"qualifying license. The API safety rail returns HTTP 403 with the message"
" *\"creating more than 1 self-service agent(s) requires an E20 or "
"Enterprise license\"* for any over-limit creation attempt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:73
msgid ""
"**With a multi-LLM license**, agent creation is unlimited (subject to "
"permissions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:75
msgid ""
"For the full feature/license matrix, see [License requirements"
"](/administration-guide/configure/agents-admin-guide.html#license-"
"requirements) in the Admin Guide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:77
msgid "Creating an agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:79
#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:139
#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:167
msgid "Open the **Agents** page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:80
msgid ""
"Select **Create agent**. A full-page editor opens with three tabs: "
"**Configuration**, **Access**, and **MCPs**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:81
msgid "Fill in the tabs (see below). Required fields are validated when you save."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:82
msgid ""
"Select **Save**. The plugin creates a Mattermost bot user, persists the "
"agent record, propagates the change to other cluster nodes, and returns "
"you to the Agents list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:84
msgid ""
"![Agents page showing the All agents tab and Create agent button.](../img"
"/managing-agents-overview.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:84
msgid "Agents page showing the All agents tab and Create agent button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:86
msgid "Configuration tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:88
msgid ""
"The Configuration tab covers identity, model selection, custom "
"instructions, and per-agent capability toggles. The fields that appear "
"depend on the AI service you select."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "Field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Display name**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Required. The user-facing name shown in posts, the agent list, and the "
"RHS picker. Updating the display name also updates the linked Mattermost "
"bot's display name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Agent username**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Required. The `@mention` handle for the agent. Must start with a letter "
"and contain only lowercase letters, numbers, periods, hyphens, and "
"underscores. Maximum 22 characters in the UI. The server-side validator "
"does not enforce a length limit; direct API callers are constrained only "
"by the database schema (`VARCHAR(64)`). **The username is set when the "
"agent is created and cannot be changed afterward.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Agent avatar**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Optional. Upload a custom image. Avatar upload is a second step after the"
" agent record is created or updated; if the avatar upload fails the rest "
"of the save still succeeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**AI Service**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Required. Pick a configured service from the dropdown. Services are "
"managed in **System Console > Plugins > Agents** and shared across "
"agents. If the agent references a service that has been deleted, an "
"\"Unknown service (deleted)\" entry appears in the dropdown until you "
"pick a new one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Model**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Optional. Override the service's default model for this agent. For "
"OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, OpenAI Compatible, Gemini, and Vertex AI "
"services the field becomes a combobox populated by a live model fetch "
"from the provider; for other services it is a free-text field. Leave "
"empty to use the service default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Custom instructions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Free-text. Prepended to every request as the agent's system prompt. Use "
"it for tone, role, vocabulary, or workflow guidance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Enable Vision**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Available for service types that support image input. Lets the agent "
"process attached images. Requires a vision-capable model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Enable Tools**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Available for service types that support tool calling. When off, the "
"agent runs without tools and the **MCPs** tab is disabled. Some "
"Mattermost Agents features will not work without tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Native provider tools**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Available when the selected provider exposes native tools (Anthropic, "
"OpenAI on Responses API, Gemini, Vertex AI, and OpenAI Compatible/Azure "
"when **Use Responses API** is on). Pick which native tools (such as web "
"search) the agent may use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Reasoning**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Available for Anthropic, OpenAI (Responses API), Gemini, and Vertex AI "
"services. Lets you enable extended thinking and pick a reasoning effort "
"or thinking budget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid "**Structured Output**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md
msgid ""
"Available for Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenAI Compatible, and Azure services. "
"When enabled and a JSON schema is supplied at request time, the model "
"returns valid JSON matching the schema. For Anthropic services, "
"**Structured Output** and extended thinking cannot be enabled at the same"
" time — turning Structured Output on temporarily disables reasoning, and "
"turning it off restores your previous reasoning setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:104
msgid ""
"Switching the **AI Service** to a service of a different type clears the "
"model field and resets the native tools, reasoning, thinking budget, and "
"structured output fields back to defaults so you don't carry stale "
"provider-specific values across providers. Switching between two services"
" of the same type (for example two OpenAI Compatible entries) preserves "
"those fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:106
msgid ""
"If the form is invalid when you select **Save**, validation errors are "
"shown inline (display name required, username required and must match the"
" allowed pattern, AI Service required) and the editor returns to the "
"Configuration tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:108
msgid "Access tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:110
msgid ""
"The Access tab controls who can interact with the agent and who can "
"administer it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:112
msgid ""
"**Channel access** restricts the channels in which the agent can be "
"`@mentioned`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:113
msgid ""
"**All channels** (default): the agent works in every channel where it is "
"a member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:114
msgid "**Allow only**: the agent only responds in the channels you list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:115
msgid "**Block**: the agent responds everywhere except the channels you list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:116
msgid "**None**: the agent cannot be used in channels at all (DM-only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:117
msgid "**User access** restricts which users can interact with the agent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:118
msgid "**All users** (default): anyone in the workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:119
msgid "**Allow only**: only listed users, or members of listed teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:120
msgid "**Block**: everyone except listed users or members of listed teams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:121
msgid ""
"**Agent admins** is a list of users who can edit and delete this agent in"
" addition to the creator. The agent creator is always an admin and is not"
" shown in the editable list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:123
msgid ""
"These rules are enforced both for `@mentions` in channels and for direct "
"conversations with the agent. They are enforced in the server in "
"`bots/permissions.go`, so they apply uniformly to UI flows, slash "
"commands, and tool-driven access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:125
msgid "MCPs tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:127
msgid ""
"The MCPs tab is available only when **Enable Tools** is on (Configuration"
" tab). It controls which MCP tools the agent may call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:129
msgid ""
"**Automatically enable all MCP tools**: the agent has access to every MCP"
" tool available in the server right now and to any MCP tools added later."
" This is the default for new agents and the setting used by all migrated "
"legacy bots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:130
msgid ""
"When the auto-grant is off, pick the specific MCP tools to enable. Tools "
"that are no longer present on the server are dropped from the agent's "
"allowlist when you save."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:131
msgid ""
"For OAuth-backed MCP servers, you can also start the per-user **Connect**"
" flow directly from this tab. Enabling a server that is currently "
"disconnected stores a wildcard grant — once you finish the OAuth flow, "
"the agent gets every tool that server exposes. The tab refreshes "
"automatically when you connect or disconnect (`mcp_connection_updated` "
"websocket event)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:133
msgid ""
"Per-tool **approval policies** (`ask`, `auto_run`, `auto_run_everywhere`)"
" are configured by an administrator in **System Console > Plugins > "
"Agents > Model Context Protocol (MCP) > Tools**. Granting a tool to an "
"agent on the MCPs tab does **not** override those policies — runtime "
"approval still applies. For more on the approval model, see [Multiplayer "
"Tool Calling](multiplayer_tool_calling.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:135
msgid "Editing an agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:137
msgid "To edit an agent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:140
msgid "Select the row, or open the row's `⋯` menu and choose **Edit**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:141
msgid ""
"Update fields across the three tabs as needed. The editor opens on the "
"**Configuration** tab and remembers your tab selection while editing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:142
msgid "Select **Save**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:144
msgid ""
"The editor uses a full-document `PUT /agents/:id` save, so every visible "
"field on every tab is sent on save. There is no per-field partial update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:146
msgid "What's editable vs locked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:148
msgid ""
"**Display name**, **avatar**, **service**, **model**, **custom "
"instructions**, **vision**, **tools**, **native tools**, **reasoning**, "
"**structured output**, **channel access**, **user access**, **agent "
"admins**, and the **MCP tool grants** can all be changed at any time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:149
msgid ""
"**Agent username is permanent.** Once the agent is created, the username "
"field is disabled in the editor. The Mattermost bot account is keyed off "
"this username, and changing it would orphan existing `@mentions` and "
"conversation history. To use a different username, create a new agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:151
msgid "Unsaved-changes warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:153
msgid ""
"If you have unsaved changes and try to leave the editor — by selecting "
"**Cancel**, pressing **Escape**, or selecting the back arrow — Mattermost"
" shows a **Discard changes?** confirmation with **Discard** and **Keep "
"editing** buttons. **Discard** abandons your edits and returns to the "
"Agents list. **Keep editing** dismisses the prompt and leaves you in the "
"editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:155
msgid ""
"The dirty-state check considers both form fields and a queued avatar "
"upload, so swapping the avatar but making no other change will still "
"trigger the warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:157
msgid "Effect of edits on running conversations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:159
msgid ""
"Updating the agent's display name flows through to the linked Mattermost "
"bot's display name immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:160
msgid ""
"Updating the AI service, model, or instructions takes effect on the next "
"agent turn — in-flight responses already streaming to a user are not "
"interrupted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:161
msgid ""
"Updating channel/user access rules takes effect immediately for new "
"mentions; the next time a user `@mentions` the agent in a channel that is"
" now blocked, the agent will refuse the request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:163
msgid "Deleting an agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:165
msgid "To delete an agent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:168
msgid "Open the row's `⋯` menu and select **Delete**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:169
msgid "Confirm in the **Delete agent** dialog. The action cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:171
msgid "Deleting an agent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:173
msgid "Soft-deletes the row in `Agents_UserAgents` (sets `DeleteAt`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:174
msgid ""
"Deactivates the linked Mattermost bot account, so `@mentions` no longer "
"route to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:175
msgid ""
"Publishes a cluster event so every Mattermost node refreshes its bot "
"cache, and broadcasts a `bots_invalidate` websocket event so connected "
"webapp clients drop the agent from their pickers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:177
msgid ""
"Existing posts that mention or were authored by the agent remain in "
"channels with their original content; only the agent's ability to reply "
"to new requests is removed. Custom prompts that referenced the agent by "
"username may no longer resolve that agent after deletion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:179
msgid "Legacy bot migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:181
msgid ""
"Mattermost Agents V1 stored bot definitions inline in the plugin's "
"`config.bots` array in `config.json`. V2 moves agents into the database. "
"To make this transition automatic, the plugin runs a one-time migration "
"on startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:183
msgid "What happens on upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:185
msgid ""
"When the v2 plugin first activates against a server that previously used "
"v1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:187
msgid ""
"The plugin acquires a cluster mutex (`ai_legacy_bots_migration`) so only "
"one node performs the migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:188
msgid ""
"It reads the stored config and, for each entry in `config.bots` that is "
"not already represented in `Agents_UserAgents`, creates a new agent "
"record. The existing Mattermost bot user account is reused; only the "
"agent record is new."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:189
msgid ""
"Each migrated agent is created with `AutoEnableNewMCPTools = true` so it "
"preserves the legacy \"all tools allowed\" behavior. The MCP tool "
"allowlist is not carried over from any prior gate because v1 bots had "
"access to every MCP tool by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:190
msgid ""
"Each migrated agent has an **empty `CreatorID`** and an **empty admin "
"list**. This is what marks them as legacy. Any system administrator "
"(`manage_system`) can edit or delete migrated agents from the Agents "
"page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:191
msgid ""
"The plugin clears `config.bots` from the stored configuration to prevent "
"duplicate bot registration on the next run, and writes "
"`legacy_config_bots_migrated = true` to the system table so the migration"
" does not run again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:193
msgid "Soft-deferred migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:195
msgid ""
"If a config bot exists but its corresponding Mattermost bot account isn't"
" yet registered (which can happen during a fresh plugin enable that "
"occurs before the bot owner runs `EnsureBots`), the migration **defers** "
"instead of creating partial records:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:197
msgid "No agents are created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:198
msgid "`config.bots` is **not** cleared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:199
msgid "The migration flag is **not** set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:200
msgid ""
"A warning is logged: *Deferring legacy bot migration: Mattermost bot not "
"found*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:202
msgid ""
"The migration retries on the next config update or plugin reload. This is"
" the expected behavior for e2e and fresh-install scenarios — no operator "
"action is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:204
msgid "How to verify migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:206
msgid "After upgrading:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:208
msgid ""
"Open the **Agents** page. Each pre-existing v1 bot should now appear as "
"an agent row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:209
msgid ""
"Open **System Console > AI Bots**. You should see the **AI bot "
"configuration has moved** notice with a link to the Agents page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:210
msgid ""
"Confirm in the database that `Agents_UserAgents` contains the expected "
"number of rows and that `config.bots` is empty in the stored plugin "
"configuration. Use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:217
msgid ""
"Confirm that the system value `legacy_config_bots_migrated` is set to "
"`true`. The flag lives in the plugin-owned `Agents_System` table — there "
"is no `mmctl` command for plugin-specific system tables, so this check is"
" SQL-only:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:222
msgid ""
"If migration was not performed (because no `config.bots` entries existed)"
" the flag is **not** set; the plugin will check again the next time "
"configuration changes. This is intentional: enabling the plugin on a "
"clean instance and then importing bots later should still trigger the "
"one-time migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:224
msgid "Backups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:226
msgid ""
"`Agents_UserAgents` is a plugin-owned table and is included in standard "
"Mattermost database backups. Plain `mattermost-config.json` snapshots are"
" no longer sufficient to restore agents — they contain only services and "
"the default-bot setting, not agent definitions. See [Backup and "
"restore](../admin_guide.md#backup-and-restore) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:228
msgid "HA cluster behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:230
msgid ""
"Agent changes propagate across Mattermost cluster nodes through two "
"channels: a plugin cluster event and a webapp websocket broadcast."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:232
msgid "When an agent is created, edited, or deleted on any node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:234
msgid ""
"The node that handled the request **refreshes its own bot cache**, "
"calling `EnsureBots()` so the new or changed agent is loaded into memory "
"immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:235
msgid ""
"The plugin **publishes an `agent_update` cluster event** using "
"`model.PluginClusterEventSendTypeReliable`. Every other plugin node "
"receives it via `OnPluginClusterEvent` and triggers the same forced "
"refresh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:236
msgid ""
"The plugin **broadcasts a `bots_invalidate` websocket event** to all "
"connected clients (`custom_mattermost-ai_bots_invalidate`). Webapp "
"clients invalidate their RHS bot picker cache and refetch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:238
msgid ""
"The same channels carry plugin **config updates** (`config_update` "
"cluster event) so service changes made in one System Console session are "
"picked up cluster-wide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:240
msgid "Practical consequences:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:242
msgid ""
"Agent changes are visible cluster-wide within seconds. There is no need "
"to restart the plugin or stagger updates across nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:243
msgid ""
"If the cluster event is dropped (for example because a node briefly "
"leaves the cluster), the next config or plugin reload on that node forces"
" a fresh DB load, so agents will not stay stale indefinitely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:244
msgid ""
"The migration mutex ensures that legacy bot migration runs on exactly one"
" node even when several nodes start simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:246
msgid ""
"`EnsureBots()` is called during `OnActivate()` (`server/main.go:220`), so"
" a node that never receives an `agent_update` event will still load DB-"
"backed agents on startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:248
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:250
msgid "\"Self-Service Agents\" upgrade screen is shown instead of the agents list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:252
msgid ""
"The server does not have a multi-LLM license applied. Apply an Entry, "
"Enterprise, or Enterprise Advanced license in **System Console > About > "
"Edition and License** to unlock the Agents page. There is no UI path to "
"create the single free-tier agent permitted by `FreeTierAgentLimit`; that"
" limit is an API-only safety rail and direct API access would be required"
" to use it (not typical for end users)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:254
msgid "\"Create agent\" button is hidden"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:256
msgid ""
"The signed-in user does not have `manage_own_agent` or `manage_system`. "
"Grant `manage_own_agent` through your role/permission configuration, or "
"sign in as a system administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:258
msgid "\"Edit\" and \"Delete\" actions are not shown for an agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:260
msgid ""
"The signed-in user is not the agent's creator, not in **Agent admins**, "
"and does not have `manage_others_agent`. For migrated legacy bots (no "
"creator), only system administrators see these actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:262
msgid "Agent shows \"Service unavailable\" badge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:264
msgid ""
"The agent's `serviceID` no longer matches any service in **System Console"
" > Plugins > Agents**. Edit the agent and pick a current service from the"
" dropdown, or restore the missing service in System Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:266
msgid "Saving an agent returns \"This username is already taken\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:268
msgid ""
"Another agent (active or recently deleted) already uses the username. "
"Pick a different username. Usernames cannot be changed after creation, so"
" attempting to edit the conflicting agent is not a workaround — delete "
"that agent if it is truly unused, or pick another name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:270
msgid ""
"Saving an agent returns \"creating more than 1 self-service agent(s) "
"requires an E20 or Enterprise license\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:272
msgid ""
"You are at the free-tier limit and the server does not have a multi-LLM "
"license. Apply a qualifying license, or delete the existing agent before "
"creating a replacement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:274
msgid "Avatar didn't update after save"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:276
msgid ""
"Avatar upload runs as a second request after the agent record is saved. "
"If the avatar upload fails (network blip, image too large, unsupported "
"format), the agent record is still saved successfully but the avatar is "
"unchanged. Re-open the editor, re-select the file, and save again. Avatar"
" upload enforces a 10 MB maximum size. There is no content-type pre-"
"validation in the plugin; the Mattermost server's profile image "
"processing handles format checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:278
msgid "Editor shows the previous agent's avatar after switching agents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:280
msgid ""
"This was a known issue (MM-68531, fixed in PR #690). If you observe this "
"on a v2.0 build, confirm the plugin version includes that fix and refresh"
" the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:282
msgid "MCPs tab is grayed out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:284
msgid ""
"The agent has **Enable Tools** turned off in the Configuration tab. Turn "
"it back on to access MCP configuration. Some product features (channel "
"summaries with tool-backed actions, tool-using custom prompts) will not "
"work for this agent until tools are enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:286
msgid "MCP server is shown but tools list is empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:288
msgid ""
"For OAuth-backed MCP servers, each user must complete the OAuth flow "
"before tools are visible. Use the **Connect** button on the MCPs tab — or"
" in the Agents RHS **Tools** popover — to start the flow. Until you "
"connect, you can still toggle the server on; this stores a wildcard grant"
" so the agent gets every tool the server exposes once you authenticate. "
"See [OAuth-backed MCP servers](../admin_guide.md#oauth-backed-mcp-"
"servers) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:290
msgid "Agent change isn't visible on another cluster node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:292
msgid ""
"Cluster propagation is fast but not synchronous. Wait a few seconds and "
"refresh the Agents page on the other node. If the agent still doesn't "
"appear, check the plugin logs on that node for *Failed to re-ensure bots "
"after agent update cluster event* or *Failed to publish agent update "
"cluster event* — both indicate the cluster event channel itself is "
"unhealthy. A plugin reload on the affected node forces a fresh DB load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:294
msgid "Cannot delete a migrated legacy bot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/features/managing_agents.md:296
msgid ""
"Migrated legacy bots have no creator and no agent admins, so only system "
"administrators (`manage_system`) can delete them. Sign in as a system "
"administrator and try again."
msgstr ""

